{title: We Gather Together}
{artist: Dutch hymn / trans. Theodore Baker}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: D}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: we-gather-together.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
We [D]gather to[G]gether to [D]ask the Lord's [A]blessing
He [D]chastens and [G]hastens His [A]will to make [D]known
The [Bm]wicked op[Em]pressing now [D]cease from dis[A]tressing
Sing [D]praises to His [G]name; He for[A]gets not His [D]own
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Be[D]side us to [G]guide us, our [D]God with us [A]joining
Or[D]daining, main[G]taining His [A]kingdom di[D]vine
So [Bm]from the be[Em]ginning the [D]fight we were [A]winning
Thou, [D]Lord, wast at our [G]side, all [A]glory be [D]Thine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
We [D]all do ex[G]tol Thee, Thou [D]Leader tri[A]umphant
And [D]pray that Thou [G]still our De[A]fender wilt [D]be
Let [Bm]Thy congre[Em]gation es[D]cape tribu[A]lation
Thy [D]name be ever [G]praised! O [A]Lord, make us [D]free
{end_of_verse}
